  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobilising Finance for Forests</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Key objective of the Mobilising Finance for Forest Program (MFF) is to mobilize private capital to protect and restore tropical forests.  Specifically, it aims to:
i. De-risk investment into projects that have high mitigation potential and strong co-benefits for biodiversity, vulnerable communities, and economic development.
ii. Improve bankability of MFF investees with the provision of technical assistance (TA).
iii. Promote the development of blueprints to significantly accelerate commercial investment into Forests and Sustainable Land Use (FSLU) projects in tropical landscapes of target countries.
iv. Create an example of a bankable FSLU portfolio with balanced risks and high impact.</narrative>
  </description>
